on on godot-cpp, or remove our godot-cpp CI test.\r\n> I'll disable it for now to unblock `master`.\r\n\r\nHm, I don't think we should tag a Godot 4.6 release, that'll just muddy the waters for godot-cpp versioning.\r\n\r\n@bruvzg:\r\n\r\n> I guess in this case, we can keep copies of `extension_api.json` for each stable release in the main repo instead of downloading it from `godot-cpp` (#109420, will need updating).\r\n\r\nAnother option is having the CI pull the actual Godot binaries for those versions and running `godot --dump-extension-api`?\r\n\r\nThat has the advantage that we aren't putting huge files in Godot's git repo, and aren't depending on what godot-cpp does. But it has more ways to fail given that it's not _just_ a file download\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3800702892/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3800758638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115389#issuecomment-3800758638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115389","id":3800758638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iivlu","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_ur